# Garry configuration. Copy this file to .env.local in the repository root
# (cp .env.example .env.local) and fill in what you need. Every variable is
# optional. .env.local is never committed (see .gitignore) and wins over .env.
# The garry CLI and garry serve read both files from the folder they run in.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Fine grained personal access token (github.com, Settings, Developer settings,
# Personal access tokens, Fine-grained tokens). Repository access: only the
# repositories Garry works on (this one for "Propose to team", plus the service
# repositories for garry ws pr). Permissions: Contents and Pull requests, both
# Read and write. Used by: garry ws pr, garry skills propose, the Skills page
# (Propose to team) and the Pull requests page (live state and checks).
GARRY_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Instead of a token here you can connect in Garry (Build, Import from GitHub, or
# garry github login): the token is saved in ~/.garry/github.json. Signed in with
# the GitHub CLI (gh auth login)? Garry uses that too.

# A GitHub OAuth app's client id (Settings, Developer settings, OAuth Apps, with
# "Enable Device Flow" on). With it, connecting is a code you enter on github.com
# instead of pasting a token.
# GARRY_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=

# GitHub API base, only for GitHub Enterprise Server
# (for example https://github.example.com/api/v3).
# GARRY_GITHUB_API=https://api.github.com

# The repository skills are proposed to, as owner/name.
# Default: the origin remote of this checkout.
# GARRY_SKILLS_REPO=piotrgodycki/garry

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Skills
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# "ci-only" turns local skill installs off: a skill then reaches the agents only
# through a reviewed pull request. Default: local (installs allowed).
# GARRY_SKILLS_POLICY=local

# Where locally installed skills live. Default: ~/.garry/skills
# GARRY_SKILLS_HOME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server and devices
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Garry's own data: paired devices (devices.json) and the sample registry copy.
# Default: ~/.garry
# GARRY_HOME=

# Extra browser origins allowed to write to garry serve, comma separated, when
# the dashboard runs somewhere other than garry serve or the dev server
# (http://localhost:3000).
# GARRY_UI_ORIGINS=

# The dashboard's API server, when it is not the server that serves the page.
# Leave unset: garry serve and the dev server (pnpm dev) handle it.
# VITE_GARRY_SERVER=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PR screenshots (garry shots)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A Chromium to use instead of the one Playwright downloads.
# GARRY_CHROMIUM_PATH=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not here: GitHub repository secrets (Settings, Secrets and variables, Actions)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NPM_TOKEN                 publishes the garry package to npm (release.yml)
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN   AI code review on pull requests (code-review.yml),
#                           from "claude setup-token" on a Claude Pro or Max plan
# Repository variables: NPM_TRUSTED_PUBLISHING=true, GARRY_REVIEW_MODEL
